  "2026-07-06T22:23:28.812Z",codex,"Creation evidence: live pm --help --json lists test-runs-worker as a top-level subcommand with description 'Internal background worker command'; pm contracts --flags-only --json also includes it in the command list. pm search --status all for test-runs-worker/internal worker/help surface found no focused open item; existing hits were broad/closed help or coverage work. This item keeps the worker reachable for orchestration but removes it from the default agent-facing command budget."
  "2026-09-12T07:07:34.409Z","harness:codex","Live source already hides the legacy worker. Complete the explicit plumbing route as item test worker, preserve the orchestration alias, and prove internal tier propagation prevents discovery under the public item test parent."
  "2026-09-12T07:52:25.363Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: item test worker is hidden beneath its public parent even with --all, remains explicitly inspectable with its required runId and no local flags, and retains test-runs-worker compatibility. Runtime discovery excludes internal commands by default but restores them through --full or exact command selection; 134 executable refusal probes passed including independent worker paths."
  "2026-09-12T07:57:25.680Z","harness:codex","TDD finding and fix: a new SDK assertion reproduced five unsupported worker flags (--status/--limit/--stream/--tail/--force) inherited from the public test-runs table. The worker now exposes inherited globals only in the shared flag contract, matching its real Commander and runtime-contract surface. Static quality caught runContracts complexity 18 over ceiling 16; shared visibility selection now uses a reusable predicate and the unchanged CodeFactor-parity ceiling passes."
  "2026-09-12T09:18:28.122Z","harness:codex","Final acceptance: item test worker remains executable and internal; explicit contracts report the required runId and no unsupported local flags; legacy orchestration spelling is retained. Full 8752-test suite and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage passed, including canonical and legacy worker discovery and refusal probes."
